Overpay and get the difference refunded!
Nanjing real estate market sees "difference compensation" again - CNTV
XINHUA DAILY PRESS OF YANGZI NEWS (Reporter Ma Zhubo) reported on Monday that after being absent for over a decade, "price protection agreements" have returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property in the New District of Jiangbei claimed to offer "difference compensation," stating that the discounts on other properties before handover were greater than previous discounts, and the developer was willing to exchange houses for buyers and refund the difference.
"Terms of Valued Consignment" are not few
The property located in the New District of Jiangbei is called Poly Yanziyu Cloud Terrace. Mr. Sun, who was viewing the property, told the reporter that he found a "statement" last weekend when he was browsing the property.
The pictures sent to the journalists show that the developer of the楼盘 has promised that anyone who purchases a property unit between February 1st and February 28th will be eligible for a swap and receive a refund of the difference in price if other unsold properties within the project offer greater discounts than those they received when purchasing their unit (limited to other units of the same户型, in the same栋, in the same单元, and of the same物业类型 that have not been sold). This can be done from the date of signing the sales contract until the corresponding property is delivered.
Sun said that real estate agents described it as a "price-lock agreement," aimed at making buyers feel secure in their purchase and not worrying about the developer lowering prices for promotional sales. "Now they're afraid that once they buy, it will be discounted. Go to the sales office to make a fuss there is no time, and not making a fuss also feels uncomfortable."
Still, others believe that while a “price-lock agreement” does provide buyers with a sense of security, the conditions attached are not low.
Ms. Zheng, who plans to buy a first-time home in North Jiangnan, says that for insured listings, the first priority is the same floor plan, followed by the same building and unit. With so few comparable options available, the "barrier" remains quite high.
There are also buyers who argue that it is difficult for them to "seek redress" when purchasing properties due to asymmetry of information, as sellers may not exclude the possibility of offering additional discounts during sales.
Whether buyers can be retained remains to be seen.
The reporter learned from Nanjing Online Real Estate that the project obtained sales permits for two buildings totaling 252 units last November, with户型sizes ranging from 105 sqm, 114 sqm, and 129 sqm, and a full-furnishing sales permit均价of 39,843 yuan per sqm.
However, just two months later, online real estate shows that the total unsold units of this project currently stand at 157, accounting for 62.3%, with 128 units in Tower 8 having 113 unsold and 124 units in Tower 7 with 44 unsold. The total number of sold units is only 33, accounting for just 13%.
Market participants explain that "price protection agreements"也曾 appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the housing project Xiangtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road West in He Xi had launched the "Price Guarantee Plan" to attract homebuyers. The details were as follows: "The company solemnly promises that if there is an increase in the discount within one year, any resulting difference will be refunded to the original owners."
In April 2011, nine more housing projects in Nanjing also offered some units with a “difference refund” promise.
The real estate market is warming up, and now more than ever requires a ‘shot of adrenaline.’
Mr. Shen, a seasoned property developer in Nanjing, stated, "Price-lock agreements" are also one of the marketing strategies used by real estate developers.
He believes that enterprises now need more confidence than homebuyers do, and that offering a “price-lock agreement” is essentially giving them a boost.
Regarding whether he can retain homebuyers, he says this depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, and it remains to be seen at this point.
Chinese rescue teams continue to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and have rescued four trapped individuals - Xinhua.
Xinhua News Agency February 11 – According to a notice on the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on February 11, China's rescue team, which was searching in Turkey, dispatched three operational teams and 45 rescuers on February 10, rescuing one person who was trapped.
Dispatched two search assessment teams to evaluate and investigate 15 buildings on Voddabash Street.
So far, 4 people have been rescued, 5 bodies have been found, and life signs and risks assessments have been conducted on 25 severely damaged buildings.
The rescue forces will adjust their rescue efforts scientifically based on the actual conditions of the disaster area and the site, and continue to conduct rescue operations in depth.
The rescue team obtained rescue request information through embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, among others, and verified each case through online inquiries and on-site searches.
Brief the Chinese Hong Kong rescue team on the current rescue environment and conditions of building collapses, and conduct joint search operations.
Currently serving as the Regional Coordination System (SSC5) with the Italian rescue team, and dispatching three members to work at the 5th RescEU Coordination Center. Communicating with multiple teams from countries including Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, and Oman, I have gained an understanding of the rescue operations conducted by both the UN rescue organization and various national rescue teams.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and force support, adhering to the principle of "unified command, safety first," enhancing safety control at the rescue site, reinforcing requirements for rescue work discipline, and specifying safety precautions.
Maintain a rotating on-duty and sentry system to strengthen camp security management.
Medical personnel from the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the队员们, strengthen medical safeguards for key personnel, and currently all members of the rescue team are healthy. They are also conducting camp disinfection.
After the camp was established,后勤保障队员 erected a total of 26 portable tents in four categories: command and communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, living accommodation, and kennels, to ensure the provision of over 30 sets of rescue equipment at the scene.
Kim Jong-un's daughter interacts closely with his father, while his wife is left on the side.
(Comprehensive 11th Edition) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on Sunday evening, with Kim Ji-won, the leader Kim Jong-un's daughter, not only attending but also standing alongside her father on the rostrum.
North Korean state media released footage on Sunday showing Kim Jong-un hugging his father affectionately, looking at him tenderly and whispering to him several times. She held her father's face with her hands and even touched his chest. The father-daughter interaction was broadcast throughout the country.
However, First Lady Li Xueju could only step aside.
According to reports from South Korea’s “Chosun Ilbo” among others, Kim Jong-un and Lee Seo-joo’s daughter Kim Jong-ae attended an official photo taken on the evening of July 7th, where she was notably seated in the middle C position between her parents. The following day, on the 75th anniversary of the founding of the People’s Army, she was seen alongside Kim Jong-un on the reviewing stand.
North Korean state media, CCTV of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, later released footage of the parade, revealing more scenes of father-daughter affection.
Kim Jong-un looked several times at his daughter on the dais, both of their smiles never fading. They whispered to each other in their ears, and Kim Chong-un once held both cheeks of his father with both hands. Kim Jong-un responded with a radiant smile.
Other state media images show that Kim Kumyeon touched her father’s face repeatedly with her hands when she sat on an indoor sofa with Kim Jong-un, and she touched Kim Jong-un’s chest with her hand as they walked arm in arm with their father.
And First Lady Li Xuequ only walked behind or sat to one side of her husband and daughter, always maintaining a few steps between them.
Korean media noted that since Kim Jong-un first appeared in public last November 18, when he tested the Hwasong-17 missile, his visibility has been increasing over the past three months, and he has now appeared at official events five times so far.
North Korean state media used the highest honorifics such as "dearest heir" and "honorable heir" when mentioning Kim Chul-ah, and aired footage of her repeatedly shouting her unwavering support for the white-headed lineage from the stands while watching the military parade.
These signs raise doubts about Kim Gu-ae’s pre-arranged succession to the Kim regime, with The Washington Post analyzing it as “a signal from Kim Jong-un elevating his middle-aged daughter to the position of successor.” However, others argue that such a conclusion is too hasty, noting that there are still various possibilities given that Kim Jong-un has a son.
"The E Fund Account is here: CSRC authorizes development, all funds under an investor's name can be aggregated and queried - Economic Observer – Professional Financial News Website."
Difficult to collect account information due to the complex channels for purchasing funds?
Always forgetting about the "slush fund"?
The issues of the villagers will soon be resolved.
February 10, the CSRC announced that the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched on various mobile app stores and is now undergoing open trial operation.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for individual investors to query information about public fund accounts and shares, aimed at addressing industry pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts or facing cumbersome querying processes.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China, managing a fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund share registration institutions, and 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration agency has an independent account system and lacks a unified industry query channel.
Industry sources indicate that at the end of 2021, China's fund investors exceeded 720 million people, meaning half of the country’s population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase status with different sales institutions separately, but with the “Fund E Account,” all purchasing situations across all销售渠道 can be checked at once, making it clear at a glance what funds they hold.
"What is the 'Fund E Account' APP?"
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed and built by the China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission, providing a one-stop query for investors on the market-wide ETFs' off-exchange holdings.
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of open-end fund shares from various fund managers across the market through the 'Fund E Account', enhancing query efficiency overall.
Specifically, investors can query through the “Fund E Account” information including: fund account information opened with all public offering fund managers, trading account information opened with public offering fund sales institutions, and the holdings of products such as open-end shares of publicly offered securities investment funds and collective asset management plans established by securities companies where the number of investors is not subject to a limit of 200 people.
Li Yuqian, head of business operations at the Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told Economic Observer that investors can get all information about their off-exchange public funds through the "Fund E Account" App in one place, helping them recover "forgotten assets." More importantly, it enables comprehensive aggregation of fund investment information across accounts for clients, allowing them to better monitor and understand their investment status in real time, accurately, and comprehensively. This helps clients optimize their fund portfolio more effectively and better plan their financial arrangements.
How to register and use?
The reporter noted that currently, the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched in the app stores of Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo, but the APP is still in an open trial operation phase, requiring users to fill in an invite code to register. Investors can obtain the invite code by contacting the fund management company they hold.
A customer service personnel from a mid-to-large-sized public fund management company in Shanghai provided an invitation code consisting of six digits to an Economic Observer reporter and said, "During the app trial run phase, China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors call to obtain them, and we provide them all."
Users will no longer need an invite code to register when open registration is activated after the trial run ends.
Please provide the Chinese text that needs to be translated.
The reporter registered and completed a query of their account by downloading and using the related documents posted on the CSRC website, which is titled "Fund E Account." The entire process took only a few minutes and mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name authentication, binding of fund accounts, and querying public offering funds.
After completing the real-name authentication, click on the "Assets" fund binding button. All fund products purchased through various fund sales platforms by the journalist will be listed in the binding option list (accounts that can be bound). After binding, one can see the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query function.
Notably, the "Fund E Account" provides query services for investors but does not facilitate subscription, redemption, or trading.
The data displayed in the "Fund E Account" generally corresponds to the date three trading days prior to the date of the query (T day).
For instance, on February 10, opening the “Fund E Account” displays the total assets, number of fund shares, and fund net value on the asset page corresponding to the three trading days before that date, which is February 7.
