Mixed data dampen Taiwan's economic start in 2023 - CNTV
Xinhua Taipei, February 11 (Xinhua reporters Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) Exports fell for five consecutive months, the manufacturing purchasing managers' index (PMI) contracted for seven consecutive months, and the consumer price index (CPI) hit "three-digit" again... In recent days, Taiwan's authorities have successively released economic data for January 2023.
Experts analyze that Taiwan's economy had a sluggish start to the year, with significant pressure on growth.
According to the Taiwan authorities' Ministry of Finance, Taiwan's exports in January this year amounted to US$31.51 billion, down 21.2% year-on-year and for the fifth consecutive month in negative growth.
The export value of the top 11 major export categories has declined compared to last year.
Rubber and plastics as well as their products, and optical equipment saw the steepest declines, falling by 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronics component exports fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Wherein, ICs declined 18.3% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 14 years.
Department of Statistics Director Cai Minna said this indicates that the softening demand in the consumer electronics industry is spreading to other parts of the electronics sector, signaling a period of correction in the industry.
Statistics show that Taiwan's imports and exports both declined in January, with a trade surplus of only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The Taiwan authorities' financial affairs department believes that reduced global end-demand, along with industry inventory adjustments suppressing purchasing intentions of manufacturers, will keep the export downturn from showing signs of improvement in the short term, potentially leading to a more severe first-quarter export decline than expected this year.
According to the Central Institute of Economic Management in Taiwan, the seasonally adjusted Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for Taiwan's manufacturing sector in January this year was 40.4%, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year and contracting for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI has 50% as its boundary line; an index greater than 50% indicates expansionary conditions, while an index below 50% indicates contraction.
In January, five components of Taiwan's PMI contracted in new orders, production, and employment, while supplier delivery times fell and inventories contracted.
Six major industries all returned to contractionary PMI readings, with contraction speeds ranked as follows: power and mechanical equipment industry (35.1%), electronic and optical industry (35.2%), chemical and biopharmaceutical healthcare industry (39.2%), basic materials industry (42.4%), transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and food and textile industry (45.7%).
Regarding prices, Taiwan’s “Statistics Bureau” reported that the year-on-year increase in CPI for January was 3.04%, once again breaching the 3% threshold since July of last year.
Whereas vegetable prices rose 28.25%, hitting a 17-month high.
Taiwan’s Statistics Bureau special committee member曹志弘 admitted that food price hikes have indeed exceeded expectations, excluding the impact of the Spring Festival, the average CPI for January and February this year should be close to 2.71% in December last year, and inflation pressure still exists and is at a high level.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts express pessimism based on reports from local media such as The联合报 and Yahoo Finance.
Professor Wu Daren from the Economics Department of Zhongbei University in Taiwan analyzed that a decline in exports could lead to cash flow problems for export manufacturing firms, increasing the risk of default on debts.
At the same time, reduced orders lead to firms cutting labor costs, which affects the labor market and household economies, thereby impacting consumption capacity.
Taiwan Economic Research Institute researcher Chiu Da-sheng believes that this year's inflation in the US and Europe has not been resolved, demand continues to shrink, and he expects Taiwan's exports to continue to decline throughout the first half of the year.
Due to Taiwan’s economy being supported by exports, its growth for the year is expected to be weaker than last year due to sluggish export performance.
New Central Committee Members, Alternate Members, and Leading Cadres at Provincial and Ministerial Levels Completing Study and Research on Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the Spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China -滚动新闻 - 湖南日报网 - 华声在线
The Graduation of the New Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Leading Cadres at Provincial and Ministerial Levels Learning and Research Class on Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the Spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China
February 11, 2023 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] Font size: [Large Medium Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 – The seminar for new members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and principal leading cadres at or above the ministerial level to study and implement Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded late yesterday afternoon at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance). Central Political Bureau member and Secretary of the Central Secretariat Cai Qi attended the closing ceremony and delivered a summary speech.
He stated that to deeply study and implement the important speech delivered at the opening of the seminar by President Xi Jinping, one must more firmly support “two establishments” and resolutely uphold “two maintenances,” enhance capabilities, and work hard in practice. One should advance the various tasks of China’s modernization in an all-round way, so as to create achievements that can withstand scrutiny from history, practice, and the people in the comprehensive building of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the all-round rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants guided by Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, studied in depth the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and President Xi Jinping's opening remarks at the seminar's start. They engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges based on actual circumstances, deepening their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues concerning China's modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the strong leadership of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core. It also heightened their sense of responsibility and mission to perform their duties, do their work well, and ensure a good start to the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, ten representatives from Seminar 1 spoke, reporting and exchanging their learning gains.
Zai Cai Qi’s statement, studying and implementing Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is both a primary political task in the current and future period, and a long-term strategic task. It should be carried out according to the requirement of “comprehensively learning, comprehensively grasping, and fully implementing.” This will push the work of studying and implementing these ideas to go deeper, more practically, and more deeply into people’s hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “two establishments,” to uphold Comrade Xi Jinping’s core position and the authority of the Central Committee of the Party and its centralized and unified leadership resolutely, and to continuously improve one’s political judgment, political insight, and political execution capabilities, always maintaining high consistency in terms of ideology, politics, and action with the Central Committee of the Party with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core.
To master well the theoretical arsenal of Marxism, to consciously arm our minds, guide practice, and advance work with the Party’s innovative theories, and to make efforts in deep study, meticulous comprehension, and sincere implementation, truly learning to be resolute in belief, absolutely loyal, and duty-bound.
To implement fully and with a proactive spirit the various decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, to advance solidly the Chinese path to modernization, to work hard and pull our sleeves up, to be down-to-earth as “construction managers,” and to turn our blueprint into reality one step at a time.
Always keep in mind that comprehensive strict governance of the Party is a never-ending journey and that self-revolution within the Party is also a never-ending journey, tightening and solidifying political responsibility for comprehensive strict governance of the Party, with party political building taking the lead, and advancing the great new project of Party building in the new era.
To enhance our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and manage and prevent risks, we must foster a strong tradition of investigation and research. We must resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Zhai Qingfeng, Li Jianjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, with Chen Xi presiding over the ceremony.
VIENTIANE – Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife had a successful official visit to Singapore and Brunei, and achieved comprehensive, practical, and specific results.
Over the course of three days during his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Van Minhang participated in more than 30 different activities.
The achievements inject new momentum for deepening, broadening, and enhancing the strategic partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand, as well as the comprehensive partnership between the two countries.
During his visit to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate Vietnam’s and the Party’s foreign policy line, which is self-reliance, diversification, dynamism, willing to be good friends and reliable partners of all countries, and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is each country’s need, aimed at enhancing the well-being of its people, and committed to peace, stability, and development in the region and the world.
At various talks and meetings, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh agreed with leaders of Singapore and Brunei to enhance political mutual trust through increased high-level delegation exchanges, effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms, and important bilateral agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among them, the Memorandum of Understanding on a Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei from 2023 to 2027 are highlights.
Vietnam signs Memorandum of Understanding on Partnership in Green and Digital Economy with Singapore.
Image from VNA
During meetings with business leaders, seminars, or attending economic forums, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh emphasized that Vietnam welcomes and creates favorable conditions for expanding investment scopes in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, and innovation and creativity by Singapore and Brunei enterprises in Vietnam.
This visit not only helps to deepen cooperation between Vietnam and Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also creates frameworks for cooperation in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
Brunei's Sultan Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister Pham Minh Duty are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Image from VNA
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made time to visit and listen to the concerns and aspirations of the Vietnamese community residing there.
In their meeting between the two leaders, Prime Minister Pham Minh Minister suggested that both governments pay more attention to ensuring fair treatment for the local Vietnamese community, provide them with opportunities to contribute to their societies, and create favorable conditions for fostering relations between the two countries.
All of these suggestions were agreed to and supported by both countries' leaders.
Specifically, Premier Pham Minh Chinh shared his desire for a united, peaceful, stable, and prosperous ASEAN community with both leaders; they agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance ASEAN’s central role in the region amid complex and multifaceted geopolitical situations.
With important achievements from his official visits to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Pham Minh Chinh contributed positively to effectively implementing Vietnam’s Thirteenth Party Congress priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors, effectively implementing the 12th Political Bureau Conclusion of the Communist Party of Vietnam on New Era Vietnamese Diaspora Work (12-KL/TW), and mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
(The end)
What exactly was the "object" that crashed over Alaska?
Muddled and disputed
The US military shot down a unidentified object flying over Alaska near its coast on Friday afternoon (February 10th) using the US' most advanced stealth fighter jet, the F-22.
The location of the downed aircraft is ten miles from the Alaskan coast.
This is the second time in less than a week that US forces have downed an airborne object.
On last Saturday, a spy balloon from China drifted over US airspace for several days before being destroyed near the coast of South Carolina in the United States.
The Pentagon said that the second object shot down entered US airspace for the first time on Thursday evening, was tracked by US military in the northeastern part of Alaska as it moved at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), and was about the size of a small car, much smaller than the previously shot-down Chinese spy balloon.
The Pentagon also believes that there are no indications at this time that the object is maneuverable.
John Kobylka, Coordinator for Strategic Communications at the National Security Council, said on Friday that while the exact appearance of the object flying at high altitude is unclear, it “poses a reasonable threat to the safety of commercial aircraft.”
Kobe stated that the object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which did not have a payload hanging from it.
Kobe said, “We call it an ‘object’ because it is the best description we can make at this point.”
President Biden consulted with the Pentagon before ordering the object to be shot down, and he made this decision “very carefully,”科比 added.
The official description of this object by the US authorities can be summarized as follows: about the size of a small car, without control sticks, without suspension systems, and flying at an altitude of around 10,000 meters.
But these pieces of information still fail to address fundamental questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what task it is performing.
Currently, many analyses and speculations online suggest that this could be another Chinese balloon.
It could be that both the spy balloon intruding into US airspace and the Chinese balloon floating over Latin America are from China, each performing some task in different locations.
Others have linked this "object" from Alaska to unidentified flying objects (UFOs).
A report in Newsweek quotes a tweet from Peter Meijer, a former US Representative, who said on Friday, "I wish this 'unidentified flying object' was actually a spy balloon, rather than a legitimate UFO."
The irony of equating alien spacecraft with weather balloons is amusing, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, Marks says.
Mayhew sent this tweet shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object over Alaska had been downed.
The Weekly News reports that it is not just Major Gray who doubts the object to be a UFO.
Republican Representative Tim Burchett of Tennessee criticized the government's cover-up of intelligence last month and demanded that the Office of the Director of National Intelligence release reports on "unidentified flying objects."
Iran Marks Revolution Anniversary as Hackers Attack President’s TV Speech
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official gathering Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but government hackers briefly interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi’s televised speech.
The president’s televised address was interrupted on the internet for about a minute, with a banner of the logo of hackers opposed to the Iranian government appearing on the screen. The group is named “Edalat Ali” (Ali Justice).
And another voice shouted “Death to the Islamic Republic.”
According to a report today by Reuters, hackers disrupted coverage of a national TV station in Iran as the country commemorated the anniversary of the revolution.
Iranian officials marked the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, with Leili’s hardline government facing the boldest challenge from young protesters demanding they step down, but Leili still called on “deceived youth” to repent so they can receive amnesty from Iran’s highest leaders.
Protests swept across Iran following the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini, who died in custody by the country's morality police in September.
Iranian security forces carried out deadly crackdowns on protests, which is one of the strongest challenges the Islamic Republic has faced since the revolution in 1979 that overthrew its 2500-year-old monarchy.
As part of a nationwide amnesty to mark the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities released on Friday two detained critics of the regime, Saeed Mehsami, who had gone on a hunger strike, and Fariba Adelkhah, an Iran-France scholar.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued a pardon that included some prisoners arrested in recent anti-government protests.
According to human rights organization HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
It is reported that 70 government security personnel have been killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for voting at Saturday’s rally to show opposition to protests and support for the government.
On the Friday night of Iran's anniversary of the Islamic Revolution, official media showcased fireworks as part of government-sponsored celebrations, and people shouted "Allahu Akbar!"
(God is the greatest!)
However, one can also hear many people shouting “Death to the dictator!” at the rally.
And the 'Death of the Islamic Republic' that was posted on social media videos.
On Saturday, government television aired live footage of official rallies across the states.
In Tehran as part of official celebrations,国产 ballistic missile interceptors, drones, anti-submarine cruisers, and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lee’s speeches are often interrupted by the slogan “Die America,” which is a标志性phrase at state rallies.
The crowd still shouted "Death to Israel."
Reuters said that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, which is a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran over the past few months.
She was sentenced to five years' imprisonment in 2020 for national security crimes.
Later they confined her at home, but in January she returned to prison.
Adelkhah denied these charges.
And just a week before Mesa was released, his supporters warned that he faced a risk of death due to a hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting mandatory headscarves.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs released Adelkhah on Friday, calling for her release and "including, if she wishes, allowing her to return to France."
