On March 29, I purchased this book through pre-order for 31 yuan, showing that it would be pushed to the device on March 31st. At that time, the Amazon website was still unable to preview the book (since it had not yet been released).
The book pushed to devices on March 31st is blank, with only "Awaiting Expectation" mentioned; meanwhile, the electronic version of the book on Amazon has been discounted to 18 yuan.
For two days, I repeatedly tried deleting the blank books downloaded from the device and resyncing, but was unable to obtain the electronic version of "The Essence of Business" that contains actual content. However, I saw that the Amazon website already allows previewing the book.
Currently, I have a few thoughts
The issue of price is not the most important; the key is how to replace the blank books on Kindle with books that actually have content now, rather than always downloading "coming soon."
The books pre-ordered should not be bought again, after all, if they fail to ship, downloading an empty-content book would look very complicated to go through.
Hope Amazon provides a normal channel for feedback on such issues, where users can report concerns about e-book downloads or usage (this could be through tickets, online customer service, etc., similar to how Microsoft’s official store handles them).
